Don't eat the lichen corpses right away, though; these don't go bad and can
be picked up and saved until you need them.  The same goes for lizard
corpses, which also have other uses.

> (I) While it is usually a bad idea to eat tripe, bats, acidic corpses
> and yellow/ purple molds, in desperate situations they are often better
> than nothing. Contrary to common sense, there's no absolutely reason
> not to eat sewer rats.

Rabid rats, on the other hand, should be steered clear of if you don't have
poison resistance... (I think these should make you sick rather than
poisoned, but whatever.)

> (K) SCMIIW, but I think some potions have a little nutritional value,
> namely water & fruit juice. Quaffing from fountains will reduce your
> hunger only some of the time.

And, in the early game when you are likely to have hunger problems, will
also be likely to get you killed.

> (K) If you have the means, poly yourself into a rock mole or umber
> hulk, and then you can eat dirt! Other monsters can make a meal of
> armour, weapons, and all kinds of other junk. Alternatively, turn ought
> to be yourself into an egg laying monster (like a female dragon), lay
> some eggs and eat them. I think there may be a penalty of some kind for
> doing this, but it beats starvation. IMHO the fact that it costs no
> nutrition to lay an egg is a bit of a bug.

YMMV, but the games where I've had polymorph and poly control in the early
game *and* have had problems with hunger, I can count on the fingers of 0
hands.

